.TH LIBRESCRS-CREDENTIALS-KDE 1 "" "LibreKDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librescrs-credentials-kde \- manage the PINs and signing key on a smart card
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librescrs-credentials-kde
.RB [ \-\-reader
.IR path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librescrs-credentials-kde
is the credential-management window of the LibreSCRS KDE integration. It
lists the PINs of the card in a reader, shows how many attempts are left,
changes a PIN and unblocks a blocked one with its PUK.
.PP
The window talks to the LibreSCRS agent (the
.B org.librescrs.Agent
D-Bus service); card access and secret entry happen in the agent, which must
be running. The smart-card plasmoid opens this window for the card it shows,
so it is normally not started by hand.
.PP
Only one window runs at a time: starting the command again raises the
existing window and, with
.BR \-\-reader ,
points it at that reader.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-reader " path"
Bind the window to the reader with this agent object path.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-author
Print the authors and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-license
Print the license and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
The LibreSCRS project: <https://github.com/LibreSCRS>
